Static Variables:

A static variable is a variable that has a static storage duration. This means that it is allocated memory at compile time and persists for the entire lifetime of the program. Static variables are initialized only once, and their values remain even after the function in which they are declared exits.

There are two main contexts in which static variables can be used:

